  "requiresBackendVersion": "0.2.1",
  "limitations": [
    "PlayFab in-process fallback supports the verified x64 40-export SDK ABI; missing device/conflict/failure UI and final upload before normal SDK cleanup are provided. Forced process termination is not a successful cloud sync. Default-on Gaming Services version metadata is not a Microsoft service implementation.",
    "Store update queries support the verified current-game no-update case; DLC, mandatory updates and downloads remain unsupported",
    "Entitled-product queries verify fresh signed Store receipts for the current game and config-declared related products, with public catalog metadata. Online access is required; other Store queries, purchase/download APIs and consumable quantities are not supplied by this increment.",
    "Installed Content discovery supports extracted PC packages with matching config/Appx identity, dependency, allowed parent and layout/file presence. It checks nearby installation directories and optional XODUS_CONTENT_ROOTS paths, not an OS-wide registry or full payload integrity. PublisherContent and content mounting remain unsupported; disk metadata never grants a license.",
    "Package license acquire/result/valid/close requires fresh verified signed proof for an installed current/related nontrial Durable package. Handles are bounded by proof/SKU expiry; lost callbacks report expiry only, not account, network or concurrency revocations. Other acquisition variants and mounting remain unsupported.",
    "Game-license change callbacks support registration, queue dispatch and safe unregistration/close. Events reflect changed verified current-title SKU receipts observed during entitlement refresh, not an OS purchase/revocation feed; initial, failed, missing or filtered observations emit no event.",
    "Incomplete XAsync cancellation/resource reclamation",
    "Partial package/event/privilege APIs are not complete GDK implementations",
    "Single HTTP/2 stream per connection; chunked uploads and proxy/client-certificate transport gaps",
    "Wine assertion observed after manual game exit; cause unresolved",
    "No multiplayer match or all-title compatibility claim"
  ]
}
